                "name": "second detail map",
                "first": "detail 2 function",
                "description": "A second detail map blended with the same technique as the base detail map: the function controls how it combines and the mask gates it by a multipurpose map channel, where white applies the detail fully and gray fades it."
            },
            {
                "name": "bump properties",
                "first": "base normal map",
                "description": "Base normal map RGB holds tangent-space normals. Its alpha interpolates between no detail normals, detail normals 1 and detail normals 2: A = none / B = detail 1 / C = detail 2, 0/0.000 85/0.333 170/0.666 255/1.000."
            },
            {
                "name": "specular properties",
                "first": "specular color map",
                "description": "Specular color map RGB tints the specular lighting highlights per pixel; the cube map reflection is left untouched. Alpha can mask the specular lighting exponent when the flag is set. Specular lighting is only enabled when the exponent is non-zero."
